  "rationale": "The frozen automatic selector inherited a reference implementation whose lag-k covariance numerator was normalized by vector energies for lag k+1. The primary Politis-White definition instead uses the sample correlogram rho-hat(k)=R-hat(k)/R-hat(0), and the authors' maintained R implementation explicitly excludes lag zero before scanning positive-lag windows. The mismatch changes selected block lengths materially in deterministic 20-condition dependent populations, which are admissible under the frozen minimum population. This correction implements the primary definition, excludes lag zero, and applies the maintained largest-significant-lag fallback. The fixed 1, 4, and 12-condition sensitivity lengths remain in every interval. No captured feature row, target, outcome, metric, candidate, threshold, prompt, economic rule, or authority was accessed or changed.",
